  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe still-frame cost of the toolpath preview is now cached. On main, an 8114-move Offset path costs the CPU 7.5-10.9 ms on each still frame. The GPU draw is about 0.2-0.3 ms before and after, so the GPU is not the cause.\n\nMain did this work again on every still frame:\n- It cloned the path and rebuilt its overlay lines (about 2.6-3.4 ms).\n- It measured all solid models again to scale the direction arrows.\n- With the operation selected or open on its page, it built the region outline twice.\n- The Pocket page note built its own region.\n- The operation page and the browser cloned the whole path to read its warnings.\n\nThe fix:\n- **Path lines** are cached for each operation. The key holds the path signature, the move count, the warnings, the palette, the background colour, the dimming and the arrow size. The arrow size is cached for each model's facets and position. The code moved out of `interact.rs` (1863 to 1797 lines).\n- **Region** is kept across frames. The key is the operation value plus `op_stamp`, never `doc_version`. The Pocket page note uses the same cache.\n- **No clones**: the new `model::with_toolpath` reads the path without a copy. The operation page and the browser use it.\n\nMain files: `crates/ui/src/path_overlay.rs`, `path_overlay_tests.rs`, `frame_memo.rs`, `egui_app/params_page.rs`, `crates/app/src/model.rs`. Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2201-toolpath-line-cache.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nCPU time for each still frame (ms), release build, 75 Hz vsync, synthetic 8114-move Offset fixture. Vsync caps the whole frame at about 13.1 ms, so the table sums the CPU timing spans.\n\n| Case | Before | After | Region builds, before / after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| none | 2.15 | 1.02 | 0 / 0 |\n| shown | 7.50 | 4.46 | 0 / 0 |\n| selected | 8.92 | 6.09 | 2 / 0 |\n| page | 8.73 | 6.14 | 2 / 0 |\n| model source: shown | 8.15 | 4.55 | 0 / 0 |\n| model source: selected | 10.88 | 6.06 | 2 / 0 |\n| model source: page | 10.80 | 6.67 | 2 / 0 |\n\nEach case is now under the 10 ms target.\n\n## Screenshot\n\nThe preview must look the same before and after. The after image is on the `screenshots` branch (commit `4a85a40e5`, `issue-2201/after-preview.png`). It was taken at an earlier head of this branch, before the final commit, and the status bar is cropped. No before image exists: the change is a cache and draws the same lines. The cache tests below compare cached lines with a fresh build.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `path_overlay_tests.rs` (four tests; none pass on main): ten still frames build no lines and measure nothing again; cached lines equal a fresh build; a new path, dimming, palette or model size each cause exactly one rebuild; a hidden path frees its cache entry.\n- `selection_frame_cost.rs`: the still-frame pin now expects 0 region builds. Main builds one for each frame, so it fails on main.\n\nQuick gate: 45 steps, 0 failed. Clippy on `camcraft-ui` and `camcraft-app` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `fig8.camproj` was not opened. All readings come from synthetic fixtures of the same size.\n- About 2-3 ms of the scene collection step has no timing span. Overlay vertex copies are the likely cause. Filed as #2653 (P7).\n\nChangelog: The toolpath preview no longer rebuilds its lines and region on every still frame, so a long Offset path draws faster.\n\nFixes #2201\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
